  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figure 8.2(b), the unweighted supermatrix for the AHP example — a screenshot titled \"Super Decisions Main Window: AHP.sdmod: Unweighted Super Matrix\". Rows and columns are grouped by cluster (L1-Goal / Goal_Node, L2-Criteria / C1-C3, L3-Alternatives / A1-A4) and every cell is printed to six decimals. Two blocks are outlined in red, which is what the caption points at: the criteria weights in the Goal_Node column (C1 0.626696, C2 0.279688, C3 0.093616) and the alternatives' local priorities under each criterion (A1 0.529640 / 0.267456 / 0.040746; A2 0.038790 / 0.583045 / 0.082529; A3 0.174103 / 0.108638 / 0.390851; A4 0.257467 / 0.040862 / 0.485875). Everything else in the visible matrix is 0.000000 — the strictly hierarchical structure AHP assumes, with no feedback between clusters.",
      "state": "draft",
